# ⚠ LOAD-BEARING BEYOND ITS SIZE. The sha256 of this submodule's built core blob IS `hearthTrueName`,
# and that value rides inside the signed preimage of every device-delegation edge. Moving this pointer
# after a founding re-binds every vessel that ever joined — each edge names a hearth true-name that no
# longer matches, and the Binding Gate refuses them all. It moves by an EPOCH ACT, never by hygiene:
# `git submodule update --remote` here is not the same gesture it is three lines above.
[submodule "TiddlyWiki5"]
	path = TiddlyWiki5
	url = git@github.com:amorphous-dreams/TiddlyWiki5.git
	branch = develop
[submodule "VSCode-TW5-Syntax"]
	path = VSCode-TW5-Syntax
